WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:10.654
In tutorial 1.6, you'll choose what's
checked each week, review your setup,

00:00:10.704 --> 00:00:11.548
and start.

00:00:12.558 --> 00:00:15.188
First, add other searches
you want to watch.

00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:17.892
You'll see your position
for each one, every week.

00:00:20.012 --> 00:00:23.752
Then choose how many pages a week
are written for your keyword.

00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:28.891
Next, turn on the growth
monitors you want.

00:00:28.891 --> 00:00:33.266
AI visibility shows how AI assistants
answer your buyers' questions,

00:00:33.316 --> 00:00:36.016
the Daily AI pulse
checks them each morning,

00:00:36.066 --> 00:00:38.968
and AI growth helps you
get named in AI answers.

00:00:39.962 --> 00:00:43.037
Then the Backlink monitor watches
the sites that link to you,

00:00:43.087 --> 00:00:45.162
the Link builder finds new ones,

00:00:45.212 --> 00:00:48.537
and the Monthly technical audit
checks your site's health.

00:00:48.587 --> 00:00:50.422
Turn off anything you don't need.

00:00:51.407 --> 00:00:54.870
At the bottom, you see the credits
all of this uses each month.

00:00:57.382 --> 00:01:00.707
Click Continue, and review
every choice in one place.

00:01:00.757 --> 00:01:03.003
Click Edit on any row to change it.

00:01:04.865 --> 00:01:07.890
Check the estimated
credits, what happens next,

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.354
and what starting now
uses from your balance.

00:01:12.907 --> 00:01:16.087
Then click Start, and your
first checks begin today.

00:01:16.137 --> 00:01:19.515
Not ready? Click Finish without
tracking, and start later.

00:01:20.886 --> 00:01:24.571
You land on your Pipeline: what
needs you, what runs on its own,

00:01:24.621 --> 00:01:26.009
and what happens next.

00:01:28.407 --> 00:01:32.894
So, choose what's checked, review your
choices, check the credits, and click Start.

00:01:35.386 --> 00:01:40.662
You're set up. Next, find your way
around Alaventra in tutorial 1.7.
